hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3136","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had cupping while he was fasting. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used cupping while he was in ihram.”"
"3137","Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam reported, saying: My uncle told us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub reported, saying: Ja’far bin Rabi’ah told me, that he heard Ikrimah says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, applied cupping while he was fasting.” Al-Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"3138","Amr ibn Yazid reported, he said: Bahz reported, he said: Shu`bah reported, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God cupped his hands.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was fasting.”"
"3139","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped his hair while he was fasting.” The two hadiths were collected by Muhammad bin Ja’far. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3140","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is the son of Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cupped while in ihram and fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3141","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said, “A fasting person in ihram cupped,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad does not take his hadith as evidence, and the arbitrator did not hear him from a divided person. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3142","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Khalaf bin Salem told us, he said: Abu Ahmad told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Divided, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, applied cupping while he was fasting and in Muharram.” Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"3143","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, saying: Qabisa narrated to us, saying: Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used cupping while fasting.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake. We do not know of anyone. He narrated it on the authority of Sufyan other than Qabisa, and Qabisa makes many mistakes. It was narrated by Abu Hashim, on the authority of Hammad, with a mursal message. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3144","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Khalaf told us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Suleiman, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “cupped He was fasting.” Maimoon bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3145","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to me, saying: Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “protected cupping while in ihram and fasting.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is reprehensible, and I do not know of anyone. He narrated it on the authority of a lover other than the Ansari, and perhaps he meant that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “married Maimuna.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3146","Humayd ibn Masada reported, on the authority of Sufyan ibn Habib, on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Maymun ibn Mihran, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “married Maimuna while he was in the same place.” He mentioned the hadith of Jabir bin Abdullah."
"3147","Ahmad bin Abi Ubayd Allah reported, saying: Abu Qutaybah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: “He was cupped while fasting.” Khalid bin Al-Harith disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3148","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khalid told us, saying: Hisham told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God cupped May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was in ihram from a garment that was on his back or on his hip. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3149","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Abu Al-Walid told us, Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was cupped while in ihram because of a fetus he had.” Al-Layth bin Sa’d disagreed with them, and he narrated it, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr. On the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3150","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was cupped while in ihram.” Mention of the hadith of Abu Sa’id (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3151","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Mukhlid bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Mu`tamir reported, he said: I heard Praiseworthy, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for the fasting person to face the qiblah and gave permission for cupping for the fasting person.” Bishr, Ismail, and Ibn Abi stopped him. Adi (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3152","Humayd ibn Masada reported, on the authority of Bishr, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, that he asked Abu Sa`id about cupping for a fasting person, He said: “There is no problem with it.” Concerning the qiblah for the fasting person, he said: “There is no problem with it.”"
"3153","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that “he did not see With the qiblah for the fasting person, there is strength for the fasting person.”"
"3154","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, that he asked Abu Sa`id about a fasting person using cupping, and he said: “There is nothing wrong with it.” The disagreement over Khaled Al-Hadha"
"3155","Ibrahim bin Saeed reported, saying: Ishaq bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, “ “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted cupping for the fasting person.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3156","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said “There is no harm in cupping for the fasting person.” Hasan bin Issa disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3157","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Isa bin Masarjis told us, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Khaled Al-Hadha told us, about Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, “He does not see any harm in cupping for a fasting person.” Qatada stopped him."
"3158","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, He said: “There is no harm in cupping for the fasting person if he does not find any weakness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3159","Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Karim reported to Abu Zar’ah al-Razi, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to me, saying: Yunus ibn Yahya narrated to me. Ibn Nubatah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Tha’labah Ibn Su’ayr, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not give up false speech, acting upon it, and ignorance, God has no need for him to give up his food or his drink.”"
"3160","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib reported, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not give up false speech and acting upon it, God has no need for him to give up his food or \His drink\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3161","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not give up false speech, acting upon it, and ignorance while fasting, God has no need of it.” To give up his food and drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3162","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever does not give up false speech, acting upon it, and ignorance when fasting, God has no need of it.” abstaining from his food and drink.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3163","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There may be a fasting person who will get nothing from his fasting except hunger, and there may be a person who is standing and will not have anything from his fasting.” He does not pray except staying up late.” Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mukharmi reported, saying: Yahya told us, meaning the son of Adam, he said: Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Usama, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the same thing. Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Saeed al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu A kitten, the same as him, but he did not raise it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3164","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Mugheerah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “Fasting is a shield. If one of you is fasting, let him not be obscene or ignorant. If someone fights him and insults him, let him say: I am fasting. \fasting\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3165","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn al-Qasim reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fasting is a shield, so if one of you is fasting, let him not be obscene or ignorant, for if someone fights him or insults him Let him say: I am fasting. I am fasting.” Abu Husayn stopped him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3166","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Husayn, whose name is Uthman bin Asim Kufi, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “If it is a day for one of you to fast, let him not be obscene or ignorant, but if it is ignorant to him, let him say: I am fasting.”"
"3167","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Salih, that he heard Abu Hurairah, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is the day of one of you’s fast, he should not be obscene and should not be noisy. If anyone insults him or fights him, Let him say: I am fasting.”"
"3168","Muhammad bin Hatim reported, he said: Suwayd reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a reading, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ata. Al-Zayat, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is a day of fasting for one of you, then he should not commit obscenities. And he should not be noisy. If someone insults him or fights him, let him say, “I am a fasting man.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ibn Al-Mubarak. Yes, and more noble with us than Hajjaj, and the hadith of Hajjaj is more worthy of authenticity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3169","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim narrated, on the authority of al-Walid, on the authority of Ibn Nimr, whose name is Abd al-Rahman. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He did not narrate On his authority other than Al-Walid, as far as we know, Al-Zuhri said: Sa’eed bin Al-Musayyab told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he says: “If one of you is reviled while he is fasting, let him say: I am fasting.” This forbids the one who is fasting."
"3170","Muhammad bin Yazid reported, saying: Ma’an told us, on the authority of Kharijah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Fasting is a protection from Hell, so whoever fasts in the morning will not be ignorant of that day, and if anyone is ignorant then there is no blame on him.” He should curse him and not curse him, but let him say, ‘I am fasting,’ by the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, because the scent of the mouth of a fasting person is better in the sight of God than the scent of musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3171","Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not be reviled while you are fasting. If someone reviles you, say: I am fasting, even if you are standing.” So sit down (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3172","Muhammad ibn Ma’dan reported, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Ayn Harrani, trustworthy, narrated to us, saying: Ma’qil narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, saying: I heard Abu Hurairah, he says: “If one of you is fasting and someone insults him, let him say: I am fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3173","Nuh bin Habib narrated, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Muammar narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God said: “Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting for Me and I will reward for it, and keeping the mouth “The fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.”"
"3174","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a reading, on the authority of Ata, he said: he narrated. Ata’ al-Zayyat, that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, because of the fear of the mouth of “The fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3175","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id informed me, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi` informed me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He continued in Ramadan, and the people continued, so He forbade them from communicating. They said: You are continuing. He said: “I am not like you. I feed and drink.” The disagreement over Al-Zuhri was mentioned in the hadith of Abu Hurairah about Al-Wasal"
"3176","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade communicating with each other. Then a Muslim man said: And you are communicating with one another, O Messenger of God. He said: “Which of you is like me?! I refused to let my Lord feed me and give me drink.” When they refused to finish, he continued with them for a day, and then another day, and then they saw Hilal, and he said: “If he had delayed, I would have done more to you,” like persecuting them when they refused to stop."
"3177","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of al-Walid, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Nimr told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Sa`id told me, And Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade the one who is connected during fasting. Some people said: You are one who is connected together, he said. “I refuse to have my Lord feed me and give me drink.”"
"3178","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abdah bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade communication out of mercy. They said: O Messenger of God, you are communicating with each other. He said: “I “I am not like any of you. My Lord feeds me and gives me drink.”"
"3179","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Laila, Habib’s grandmother, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He entered upon her and she brought him food. He said to her: “Eat.” She said: “I am fasting.” He said: “When a fasting person eats, she prays with him.” The angels are upon him until they have finished.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3180","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Sharik reported, on the authority of Habib bin Zaid, on the authority of Laila, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The fasting person When he eats, the angels pray over him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3181","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he narrates it as a narration, he said: “If If any of you wakes up on a fasting day, let him not be obscene or ignorant. And if someone insults him or fights him, let him say: I am fasting. And when one of you is invited to food while he is fasting, so let him say: I am fasting.”"
"3182","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “If one of you is called to a supplication, let him respond. If he is fasting, let him pray, and if he is not breaking his fast, let him eat.” Abu Abdul Rahman: He prays, meaning he prays."
"3183","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abtar, who is Ibn al-Qasim, Abu Zubayd, a trustworthy Kufi, told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Al-Alaa bin Al-Shakheer, on the authority of Aisha, “She fasted during Ramadan and worked hard, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to break her fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3184","Muhammad bin Amr bin Hanan Homsi reported, saying: Baqiya told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told me, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Aisha, “One day she missed the fast of Ramadan, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to make up for it.” He stayed in his place for two days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3185","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “ “I broke my fast one day, so I was ordered to make up for a day.” Or she said, “Two days.” Khaled said, “And I dare for two days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3186","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Abd al-Wahhab told us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin al-Shakhir, that Aisha fasted one day, but fasting exhausted her, so she broke her fast. Hafsa said: I will mention that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Aisha: Don’t do that until I mention it to him, so I think he ordered her to fast for a day or two. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3187","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Issa bin Yunus narrated, he said: Awf narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “If a fasting person eats out of forgetfulness or drinks out of forgetfulness, then let him complete his fast, for God only fed him and gave him drink.” Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him. He said hello, likewise (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3188","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, saying: Ali bin Bakkar told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he attributed it to the man. He eats during the month of Ramadan forgetting. He said: “God fed him and gave him drink.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith from the hadith of Muhammad bin Amr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3189","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawus On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan without sickness or sick leave, will not If he fasts it, he will make up for it by fasting for an entire lifetime.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3190","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Yahya told us, and Abd al-Rahman told us, they said: Sufyan told us, then he mentioned a word that means, on the authority of Habib, He said: Abu Al-Mutawus narrated to him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever breaks his fast on a day of... Ramadan without a sick leave or sickness, fasting for a year does not make it up for it, even if he fasts it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3191","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq and Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of al-Thawri, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan without an excuse There is no concession and he will not make it up for it, even if he fasts for the whole time.” Abd al-Razzaq said about it: “without illness.” He mentioned the difference over Shu’bah."
"3192","Mu'mal ibn Hisham reported, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Shu'bah, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Amara ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever breaks the fast on a day of Ramadan without permission God permitted it for him, and it did not suffice for him to fast for a period of time.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3193","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam Basri narrated, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Amara Ibn Umair, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Whoever breaks his fast on the day of Ramadan without permission does not make up for it by fasting for a lifetime.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3194","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu`bah reported, he said: Habib told me, he said: I heard Amara bin Umair narrates, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawus, who said: And I saw Abu Al-Mutawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan without God’s permission, that will not make up for it, even if he fasts for the whole time.”"
"3195","Hilal bin Al-Ala told me, he said: My father told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hussein, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man broke his fast during the month of Ramadan, and he came to Abu Hurairah and said: “A year’s fast is not accepted from him.” Abd stopped him. The Most Gracious, on the authority of Jacob"
"3196","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: my father told us, he said: a partner told us, on the authority of Al-Ala, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “Whoever breaks his fast on a day of Ramadan will not make it up for a day of this world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3197","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jabir told us, he said: Sulaym bin Amir told me, he said: Abu Umamah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “While I was sleeping, two men came to me and took my hyena,” and he drove Hadith, in which he said: “Then they set off with me, and behold, there were people hanging by their ankles, with their buttocks torn open and blood flowing from their buttocks. I said: “Who? These? “He said: These are the ones who break their fast before their fast begins.” He said: “The Jews and the Christians have failed.” Sulaym said: I do not know what Abu heard. An imamate from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, or something of his opinion? Brief"
"3198","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Uthman, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A woman should not fast while her husband is witness on a day other than a month.” Ramadan except by His permission.” Qutaibah bin Sa’id disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3199","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he said: “A woman should not fast while her husband is witnessing a day other than the month of Ramadan, except with his permission.” Sent by Ja’far bin Rabi’ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3200","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Shuaib bin Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman should not fast while her husband is a witness except with his permission.”"
"3201","I am Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman. He said: Ibn Wahb told us. He said: Haywa told me, and Umar bin Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Al-Haad. He said: He told me. A colleague of Urwa’s servant, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Food was given to me and Hafsa, and we were fasting, so we broke our fast, then he entered. Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so we said: O Messenger of God, a gift was given to us, and we desired it, so we broke our fast. He said: “You do not have to fast.” Another day in its place.” The disagreement over Al-Zuhri was mentioned in this hadith."
"3202","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Kathir bin Hisham narrated, he said: Ja’far bin Burqan narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, said: Hafsa and I were fasting, and food was offered to us and we craved it, so we broke our fast, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered. He greeted him, and Hafsa, who was her father’s daughter, ran to him and said: O Messenger of God, today we have been fasting in the morning, so he presented to us We craved food, so he said: “Spend another day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3203","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Yazid, who said: Sufyan bin Hussein reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: A sheep was given to Hafsa while we were fasting, and she broke her fast for me. She was her father’s daughter. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered to meet us. We mentioned that to him, and he said: “Change another day in its place.” Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, he said: We heard it from Salih bin Abi Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha and I were fasting in the morning, and a special meal was given to us. He said: And Sufyan told us, he said: And I bear witness that he They asked Al-Zuhri about Urwa? He said: No. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: What is correct is what Ibn Uyaynah narrated on the authority of al-Zuhri, and Salih bin Abi al-Akhdar is weak regarding al-Zuhri and other than al-Zuhri. Sufyan ibn Husayn and Ja`far ibn Burqan are not strong in al-Zuhri, and there is no harm in them in matters other than al-Zuhri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3204","Muhammad bin Sahl bin Askar reported, saying: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub reported, on the authority of Ismail bin Uqba, he said: And I have in another place: Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that a gift was given to her. Hafsa had food, and they were fasting, so they broke their fast with him. Hafsa, who was the daughter of Omar, asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered her to “fast one day in his place.” Yahya bin Ayyub said: I heard Salih bin Kaysan say the same thing. I found it in another place: Salih bin Kaysan told me, and Yahya bin Saeed told me the same thing, and this is also an error. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3205","Ahmad bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I and Hafsa were fasting in the morning. Food was given to us, and we liked it, so we broke our fast. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered, and she came to me. Hafsa, so she asked him, and he said: “Fast another day in its place. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: They are all wrong.” Mu’mar sent him. Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Aisha said: I have become And Hafsa, they were fasting, according to the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3206","3209 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, that Aisha and Hafsa They fasted voluntarily one day and broke their fast. Aisha said: We wanted to ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Hafsa approached me. She was her father’s daughter, so she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered her to “make up that day,” on the authority of Al-Harith bin Miskin. It was read to him and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Aisha and Hafsa, similar to him, were mursal."
"3207","Ahmad bin Issa reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Hafsa and I started fasting in the morning, and food was given to us. We liked it and broke our fast. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and Hafsa joined me. So she asked him, and he said: “Fast another day in its place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3208","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of his paternal aunt Aisha bint Talha, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon us, and we said: We have a fish that we have hidden for you. He said: “Bring it closer.” So he ate and said: “ I had wanted to fast, but I will fast another day in its place.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This wording is wrong. He narrated this hadith. A group, on the authority of Talha, but none of them mentioned, “But I will fast a day in its place.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This wording is wrong. This hadith was narrated by a group of people, on the authority of Talha, but none of them mentioned: “But I will fast another day in its place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3209","Ali bin Uthman told us, he said: Al-Mu’afa bin Sulayman told us, he said: Khattab bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon Hafsa and Aisha while they were fasting, then he left and came back while they were eating, and he said: “ “Weren’t you fasting?” They said: “Yes, but food was given to us and we liked it and we ate from it.” He said: “Fast another day in its place.” Abu said. Abdul Rahman: This hadith is objectionable and weak in hadith, and a discourse of which I have no knowledge. The correct hadith is the hadith of Muammar, Malik, and Ubaid. God (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3210","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ja’dah, on the authority of Umm Hani, who was his grandmother, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her on the day of the conquest, and a vessel was brought for him to drink. Then he gave it to me, and I said: I am fasting. He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The voluntary person is the ruler of himself, so if you wish, then fast, and if you wish, then break your fast,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ja`dah did not hear it from Umm Hani. Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna reported on the authority of Abu Dawud, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Ja’dah informed me, on the authority of his grandmother Umm Hani, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon her and mentioned the hadith. I told him: I heard it from Umm Hani’. He said: Our family told it to us, and Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, Shu’bah said: And Simmak used to say: Umm Hani’s son told me, and I narrated it on the authority of the better of them, mentioning the hadith of Simmak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3211","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ibn Umm Hani, on the authority of He heard it from his grandmother, Umm Hani, that she said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought a drink on the day of the conquest of Mecca, so he drank, then He gave it to me and I drank. I was fasting and I hated to return the surplus of his supper, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: May my father protect you, I have been fasting. He said To her: “Have you done something?” She said: No. He said: “It will not harm you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3212","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Harun bin Umm Hani, on the authority of Umm Hani, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while I was fasting, and a vessel of milk was brought to me and he drank. He gave it to me and I drank, so I said: O Messenger of God, I was fasting, but I hated to return your question. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If it is part of making up for Ramadan, then make up a day in its place, and if it is not part of making up for Ramadan, then if you want, make up for it, and if you want, do not make it up.”"
"3213","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Lahus told us, on the authority of Simmak, on the authority of Ibn Umm Hani, on the authority of Umm Hani, she said: I was She was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. A drink was brought and he drank, then he handed it to me and I drank from it. I said: I have sinned, so ask forgiveness for me. He said: “And what is that?” She said: “I was fasting, so I broke my fast.” He said: “Is it about a fulfillment that you used to fulfill?” She said: “No.” He said: “It will not harm you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3214","Ahmad ibn Uthman reported, saying: Amr told us, on the authority of Asbat, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ja`dah, on the authority of Umm Hani’, because she said that she went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he was brought a drink and he drank from it, then he handed it to her and she drank. From him, she said: I was fasting, but I hated to return your drink to you. He said: “Have you made up for it? It will not harm you.” Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Ayyub told us Yahya bin Abi al-Hajjaj, he said: Abu Yunus, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, who said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a vessel containing drink was brought. Then he gave it to me and I was fasting so I drank, something like that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3215","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Hatem told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: When the The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Mecca. The first house he entered was the house of Umm Hani’. He called for water and drank it, and Umm Hani was on his right. So he gave his surplus to Umm Hani, and Umm Hani drank it, then said: O Messenger of God, by God, I have done a good deed, and by God, I do not know. Whether I am right or not, I drank the bounty of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I was fasting. He said: “A fulfillment of Ramadan or a voluntary one?” I said: O Messenger of God, rather it is voluntary. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one who does voluntary has the option, if he wishes, he may fast, and if he wishes, he may break his fast.” He said Abu Abd al-Rahman: This hadith is confusing, and the first is like it. As for the hadith of Urwa, it is mursal and not well-known. As for the hadith of al-Zuhri Which was narrated by Ja`far bin Burqan and Sufyan bin Husayn. They are not strong in Al-Zuhri in particular, and Malik and Ubayd Allah disagreed with them. Ibn Amr and Sufyan Ibn Uyaynah, and these are more reliable and memorized than Sufyan Ibn Husayn and Ja’far Ibn Burqan. As for the hadith of Umm Hani, as there was a difference of opinion regarding Samak bin Harb regarding this matter. Simak bin Harb was not one of those who could be relied upon if he alone delivered the hadith, because he used to accept indoctrination. As for the hadith of Ja`dah, he did not hear it from Umm Hani. He mentioned it, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Umm Hani, and this Abu Salih His name is: Badhan, and it was said: Madham, and he is weak in hadith, and he is the client of Umm Hani, and he is the one from whom Al-Kalbi narrated. He said: Ibn Uyaynah. On the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said: We used to call Abu Salih Daruzan, which in Persian is a liar, except that Yahya ibn Saeed did not abandon it, and he narrated on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled on his authority, and it was narrated that he said during his illness: Everything I have narrated to you, It is a lie, and Abu Salih, the father of Suhail bin Abi Salih, whose name is Dhakwan, Thiqa Mamun, and as for the hadith of Yahya bin Ayyub, who We mentioned him, because he is not one of those who can be relied upon, and he has nothing but an objectionable hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3216","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asim bin Omar, on the authority of his father, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When night comes from here, and the day goes from here, then the fasting person has broken his fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3217","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, saying: We were with the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he was on a journey, and he said to a man: “Come down and work for us.” He said: “The sun, O Messenger of God.” Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Come down and prosper.” He said: The sun, O Messenger of God. Then he said: “Come down and prosper.” So he descended and prospered, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, drank. And he said: “If you see the night approaching from here and he points with his hand to the horizon, then the fasting person has broken his fast.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: The hadith of Asim bin Omar and the hadith of Ibn Abi Awfa are authentic. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3218","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “People will continue to be well as long as they hasten to break their fast.”"
"3219","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Yazid told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The religion continues to prevail as long as people hasten to break the fast. Indeed, the Jews delay it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3220","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah narrated, he said: Abu Qutaibah narrated, he said: Shu`bah narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Hafsa, On the authority of Salman bin Amer, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you find dates, break your fast with them, and if you do not find dates, then water. “The water is pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3221","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Salman bin Amir, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not find dates, let him break his fast with water, for water is pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3222","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Amer told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, On the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them. If he does not find them, let him break his fast with water, for it is purification.”"
"3223","I am Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali bin Muqaddam. He said: Saeed bin Amir told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them, and whoever does not, let him break his fast with water, for it is pure,” Abu Abd al-Rahman: The hadith of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, is an error, and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3224","Musa bin Hazzam Al-Tirmidhi narrated, he said: Yahya, who is the son of Adam, narrated, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Raqbah On the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Anas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to start his breakfast with dates when he broke his fast.” This hadith was narrated by him. Shu’bah, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of a mursal, and Shu’bah had better memory than the one who narrated this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3225","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, referring it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates, and if he does not find any, let him break his fast with water.” “The water is pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3226","Qutaibah bin Saeed narrated, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of her uncle Salman bin Amer informs the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If one of you breaks the fast, let him break his fast with dates, for that is a blessing. “Dates, water is pure.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This letter “is a blessing.” We do not know that anyone mentioned it other than Ibn Uyaynah. I do not think it is preserved (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3227","Ahmad ibn Harb reported, saying: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa bint Sirin, on the authority of Al-Rubaab, on the authority of Salman ibn Amer, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates, and if he does not find any, let him break his fast with pure water.” \""
3228"""
"3228","'Ali ibn Hujr informed us, saying: Qurran ibn Tammam informed us, from Hisham, from Hafsah, from al-Rabab, from her uncle Salman ibn 'Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When one of you fasts, let him break his fast with dates, or if he does not find dates, then with water, for water is purifying."""
"3229","Al-Hussein bin Muhammad told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Al-Rahih, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you break your fast, break your fast with dates, but if you do not find them, then with water, for water is pure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3230","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Salman bin Amir, he said: “ If one of you is fasting, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find dates, let him break his fast with water, for water is purification.” I, Abdullah bin Al-Haytham, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Asim told me, with this hadith, attributing it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3231","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told me, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of Salman, He said: “If one of you breaks his fast, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find dates, let him break his fast with water, for water is pure.” Hisham said: Asim Al-Ahwal told me that Hafsa attributed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3232","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan reported, on the authority of Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Abu Salih Al-Zayat, that he heard Abu Hurairah He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The fasting person has two joys that make him happy: when he breaks his fast, he rejoices in breaking his fast, and when he meets his Lord, he rejoices.” “By his fasting.”"
"3233","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of a reading, on the authority of Ata, he said: he narrated. Ata’ al-Zayyat said that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The fasting person has two joys with which he rejoices: when he breaks his fast.” He rejoices in breaking his fast, and when he meets his Lord he rejoices in his fasting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3234","Quraysh ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me. He said: Ali ibn al-Hasan informed me. He said: Al-Hussein ibn Waqid informed me. He said: Marwan informed me. Al-Muqaffa’, he said: I saw Abdullah bin Omar seizing his beard and cutting off what exceeded the palm of his hand, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he breaks his fast, he says: “The thirst has gone, the veins are wet, and the reward is guaranteed, God willing.”"
"3235","Ismail bin Masoud reported on the authority of Yazid, who was the son of Zuray’, who said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ata’ On the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prepares a invader or a pilgrim, or takes his place in his family, or breaks the fast of a fasting person.” He will have a reward similar to his, without their rewards being diminished in the least.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3236","Ali bin Al-Hussein narrated, he said: Khaled narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Zayd bin Khaled, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever breaks the fast for a fasting person will have his reward. The reward of the fasting person will not be detracted from at all.”"
"3237","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Yazid told us, saying: Husayn reported, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Whoever breaks the fast of a fasting person is He will have a reward similar to his reward, without the reward of the fasting person being detracted in any way.”"
"3238","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Suwayd narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Saeed al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “There may be a fasting person who will have nothing from his fasting except hunger, and there may be a fasting person who will have nothing from his fasting but staying up late.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3239","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad reported, saying: Muhammad bin Musa told us, saying: He recited to me, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali. Bin Hussein, on the authority of Safiyya, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “took seclusion for the last ten days of Ramadan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3240","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha. On the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, they said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seclude himself during the last ten days of the month of Ramadan until... May God take him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Jurayj disagreed with him."
"3241","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Shihab told me, about itikaf and how we practiced it, about Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that she told them, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seclude “The last ten days of Ramadan until God took his death, then his wives secluded themselves after him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by al-Layth, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, mursal"
"3242","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Saeed bin Al-Musayyab said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him He said: “He used to seclude himself during the last ten days of Ramadan until God took his life, then his wives did seclusion after him.”"
"3243","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to seclude himself during the last ten days of Ramadan until God passed away, then his wives did seclusion after him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3244","Imran bin Bakkar told me, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Aisha “used to seclude herself for the last ten days and would not enter her house except for a person’s urgent need.”"
"3245","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa narrated to me. And Umrah, on the authority of Aisha, “Whenever she would seclude herself, she would seclude herself in the mosque, and she would seclude the last ten days of Ramadan, so she did not She does not enter her house except for a person’s urgent need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3246","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He should seclude himself for the last ten days.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith was narrated by him. Muhammad bin Amr. If Muhammad bin Amr was Abu Al-Hasan, then perhaps Muhajir was Abu Al-Hasan, and he narrated on his authority. Division (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3247","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin al-Harith al-Taymi, on the authority of Abi Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to be adjacent to the ten in the middle of month, then when twenty nights have passed and the twenty-one arrives, he returns to his dwelling and whoever was living next to him returns, And he stayed in a neighboring month on that night in which he was returning, so he addressed the people and then ordered them to do what God wished, then he said: “I was I would adhere to these last ten days, and then it seemed to me that I would adhere to these last ten days. Whoever was secluded with me should remain in his seclusion, and I saw “This night, I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten days of every odd night, and you saw me prostrating in water and mud,” Abu Sa’id said. Al-Khudri: It rained on the night of the twenty-first, and it stopped raining on the mosque in the prayer area of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I looked at him as he had finished praying. In the morning, his face was wet with mud and water. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3248","Musa bin Hazzam al-Tirmidhi narrated trustworthy, he said: Yahya, who is the son of Adam, narrated, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He used to seclude himself during the last ten days of the month Ramadan, and when the year in which he died came, he secluded himself for twenty days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3249","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seclude himself during the last ten days of Ramadan, so he traveled for a year and did not seclude himself, so when the year Next, he will seclude himself for twenty days.”"
"3250","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Abu Al-Hussein Al-Rahawi narrated, saying: Miskin bin Bukayr Al-Harrani narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: narrated to us Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: It was mentioned that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He secludes himself during the last ten days of the month of Ramadan.” So she asked for his permission, and he gave her permission. Hafsa asked Aisha to give her permission, so she did. When Zainab bint Jahsh saw it, she ordered it to be built, and it was built. Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, he went to build it and saw By the buildings. He said: “What is this?” They said: “The buildings of Aisha, Hafsa, and Zainab.” He said: “Do righteous people mean this? I am not in retreat.” So he returned, and when he broke his fast, he secluded himself on the ten days of Shawwal."
"3251","Qutaybah bin Saeed narrated, and Abu Al-Ash’ath narrated Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’, and the pronunciation is his. They said: Yazid bin Zuray’ narrated. He said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “A woman from one of his wives secluded herself with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She was menstruating, and she was seeing redness and yellowness, so perhaps she put the basin under her while she was praying.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3252","Muhammad bin Mansour reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted He, peace and blessings be upon him, was to seclude himself in the first ten days of Ramadan. So Aisha asked him for permission, and he gave her permission. Then Hafsa asked her for permission, and he gave her permission. For her, and Zainab had not asked for his permission, so she heard about that and asked for permission, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, He came to his retreat, and when he prayed the morning prayer, he saw that he was four buildings away, and he said: “Who is this for?” They said: to Aisha, Hafsa, and Zainab. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You say that righteousness means this,” so he did not seclude himself during that ten days, but he secluded himself on the ten days of Shawwal. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3253","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: Amara ibn Ghaziyah al-Ansari told me, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrates, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, secluded himself during the first ten days of Ramadan. Then the middle ten secluded themselves in a Turkish dome with a piece of mat covering it. He said: So he took the mat in his hand and moved it to one side. the dome, then he raised his head and spoke to the people, so they approached him and said: “I am in seclusion for the first ten days. I will seek out this night, then I seclude myself.” The middle ten days, then I came and was told: It is in the last ten days, so whoever among you likes to seclude himself, let him seclude it.” So the people secluded themselves with him. He said And I showed her the night of Witr, and then he mentioned a word meaning “I prostrated on the morning of it in mud and water.” So it became twenty-one. He got up until dawn, and it rained, so the mosque was empty, and I saw mud and water. He came out when he finished the morning prayer with his forehead And the dung of his nose contains clay and water, and so it is the twenty-first night of the last ten nights. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3254","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath narrated, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, he said: I said, O Messenger of God, I vowed to seclude myself one night in the Sacred Mosque, and God brought Islam, so He said: “Fulfill your vow.”"
"3255","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Omar, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he asked The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, I vowed to seclude a night in the Sacred Mosque in pre-Islamic times. He said: “Fulfill \With your vow\"""""
"3256","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam narrated, saying: Muhammad bin Jaafar narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, saying: I heard Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar had set aside a day for him to seclude himself in pre-Islamic times, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. “So he ordered him to seclude himself,” mentioning the disagreement over Ayoub. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3257","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, departed from Hunayn, Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about a vow he had made in pre-Islamic times. He secluded himself for a day, so he commanded him to do so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3258","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He was on Omar vowed to seclude one night in the Sacred Mosque. “So he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to seclude.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3259","Ishaq bin Musa reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, “that there was a night in He made a vow in pre-Islamic times, so he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to seclude himself."
"3260","Abu Bakr bin Ali informed us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Hammad Al-Warraq told us, he said: Amr bin Muhammad Al-Anqazi reported, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Budayl Ibn Warqa’, on the authority of Amr Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that Omar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about itikaf, so he ordered him to to seclude himself and fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3261","Muhammad bin Khalid bin Khalili reported, saying: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ali bin Hussein informed me, Safiyya bint Huyayy told him that she had come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to visit him while he was in seclusion during the past days of Ramadan. She talked with him for an hour after dinner, then she got up and turned over, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up with her, turning her over, until... She reached the door of the mosque near the residence of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two Ansar men passed by and greeted the Messenger of God. Then they left, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: “Let your messengers go. She is Safiyya bint Huyy.” They said: Glory be to God, O Messenger of God. This was difficult for them both, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The devil takes possession of a human being to the extent of Blood, for I feared that He might put something into your hearts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3262","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, on the authority of Safiya bint Hayya, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in itikaf, so I came to visit him at night and spoke to him, then I got up and turned around, and he got up with me. Yaqalbni, and her residence was in the house of Usama bin Zaid, so two men from the Ansar passed by, and when they saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, they hurried. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “On your messengers. She is Safiya bint Huyay.” They said: Glory be to God, O Messenger of God. He said: “Indeed, Satan It flows from a person like blood, and I was afraid that he would put evil into your hearts or say something.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Sufyan bin Ayaina (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3263","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Ibn Uyaynah, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein. He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in seclusion, and Safiya came to him one night. When she returned, he walked with her at night, and a man from Al-Ansar called him and said to him: “Come, it is Safiyya. Satan flows from a person like blood.” Muhammad ibn Hatim reported, saying: Hibban reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Muammar, with this chain of transmission similar to it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3264","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Bakr, meaning Ibn Mudar, narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata’ bin Left, on the authority of a man from the Ansar, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was nearby in the mosque one day, so he preached to the people and warned them. He encouraged them, then said: “Indeed, there is no one praying except that he is in dialogue with his Lord, so do not recite the Qur’an loudly to one another.” Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam narrated, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, who said: Ibn Al-Had narrated, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim. On the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, on the authority of an Ansar man from Banu Bayyadah, that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention something similar. Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Shuaib, who said: Al-Layth narrated to us, saying: Ibn Al-Had narrated, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hazim, the client of the Ghifaris, said that this hadith was narrated to him by Al-Bayyadhi, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Abd said: The Most Gracious: Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3265","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, saying: Shu’bah reported, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Sa’id, saying: I heard Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of a man from Banu Bayyadah from the Ansar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He secluded himself on the first ten days of Ramadan, and said: “When one of you is praying, he is only speaking to his Lord, so do not raise your voices with the Qur’an,” Abu Abdul Rahman: Yahya bin Saeed disagreed with him and narrated it, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hazim (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3266","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated, saying: Ibn al-Qasim narrated, on the authority of Malik, he said: Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Hazim Al-Tammar, on the authority of Al-Bayyadi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the people while they were praying, and the They recited their voices in the recitation, and he said: “The one who is praying is speaking to his Lord, so let him see what he is speaking to Him with, and do not recite the Qur’an loudly to one another.” He said Abu Abdul Rahman: He was sent by Al-Layth bin Saeed and Yazid bin Harun. Suwayd bin Nasr reported, saying: Abdullah, who is Ibn al-Mubarak, reported on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abi Hazim, sent. Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hazim Mawla Ansar, and it was long ago that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who prays,” and he mentioned something similar. Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yahya told us, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim told him, on the authority of Abu Hazim Mawla Al-Ansar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and he mentioned something like it. Abu Abdul Rahman said: It was narrated by Ibn Numayr, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed, but he did not mention Abu Hazim. Hussein bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of a man from His people are like him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3267","Yusuf bin Saeed reported, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ziyad bin Sa’d told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa On the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that “when he secluded himself, he would not enter his house except for a person’s urgent need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3268","Abu Dawud reported, he said: Uthman told us, he is Ibn Omar, he said: Yunus reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “If I were to come to the house and there was a sick person, I would only ask while I was standing, and if the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was to enter his head over me So I would go to him, and he would not come to the house except for a need, if he wanted to perform ablution while he was in seclusion.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3269","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, “When she secluded herself, she would not ask about a sick person except while she was walking, not standing.”"
"3270","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan bin Hussein informed, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in seclusion, and he would not enter the house except for a necessary need, and I washed myself.” His head, and between me and him is the threshold of the House.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: There is no problem with Sufyan bin Hassan other than al-Zuhri, but there is no problem with him. Al-Zuhri is called Al-Qawi, and his counterpart in Al-Zuhri is Sulaiman bin Kathir and Ja’far bin Burqan, and there is nothing wrong with them other than Al-Zuhri. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3271","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he secluded himself, he would bring his head towards me and I would put his feet to him, and he would not enter the house except for a person’s need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3272","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Amra bint Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He secluded himself, bringing his head to me, so I would move it. He would not enter the house except for a person’s need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3273","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to enter his head while he was in the mosque and his feet, and he would not enter the house except for a need if he had a need. secluded"
"3274","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “ She used to go to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to bring his head to her while she was in her room and he was in the mosque.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3275","Nasr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Muammar reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “It is She used to go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while she was menstruating and he was in itikaf, and he would give her his head while she was in her room.”"
"3276","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Mansour told me, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring his head to me while he was in seclusion, so I would wash it and he would order me while I was menstruating.” \""
3277"""
"3277","Mahmud ibn Ghaylan informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to put his head out to me from the mosque while he was in i'tikaf, and he would order me to wash it, while I was menstruating."""
"3278","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring his head to me while I was menstruating, so I would wash it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3279","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to foot the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque, and he would put his head on the threshold of the room and I would foot him.”"
"3280","Amr bin Uthman reported, saying: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes to me while he is in seclusion in the mosque, and he reclines on the threshold of the door of my room, and I wash his head while I am in My room and the rest of it in the mosque.”"
"3281","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Fudayl, he is Ibn Iyaad, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Tamim bin Salamah, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to take his head out of the mosque while he was in seclusion, and I would wash it while I was menstruating.”"
"3282","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, and another mentioned, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring his head to me from the mosque while he was nearby, and I would wash it while I Menstruating.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Hisham bin Urwa, but he did not mention: and it is related to (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3283","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I was moving the head of Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was menstruating.”"
"3284","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, On the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was secluding himself in the mosque, so he would take out his head and wash it.” With marshmallow while I was menstruating.”"
"3285","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a recitation of it and the pronunciation is his, and I am listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to seclude himself during the middle ten days of Ramadan, so he secluded himself for a year until... It was the night of the twenty-first, and it was the night on the morning of which he left his seclusion. He said: Whoever secluded himself with me, let him seclude himself. the last ten days, so I was shown this night and then I forgot about it, and you saw me prostrating in water and mud that morning, so seek it on the ten days the last days, and seek it in every odd period.” Abu Sa`id said: It rained that night and the mosque was on a pergola, so the mosque was covered with water. Abu Sa`id said: Then the eyes of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw on his forehead and nose traces of mud and water from the morning of one of And twenty (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3286","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: We discussed Laylat al-Qadr with a group of Quraysh, so I went to Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who was a friend of mine, and I said: Will you not go out? Take us to the palm trees? So he came out wearing a khamisah, and I said: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention the Night of Decree? He said: Yes, we secluded ourselves with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the middle ten days of Ramadan, so we went out on the morning of the twentieth, and he delivered a speech. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “I saw Laylat al-Qadr, and I had forgotten about it, and it is in the last ten nights at an odd number, and I I saw that I was prostrating in water and mud, and whoever had secluded himself with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, let him return.” Then a cloud came and it rained until The roof of the mosque leaked and was made of palm branches. Prayer was performed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was prostrating in water and mud until I saw traces of mud on his forehead (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3287","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b said, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seclude the ten days of Ramadan, so he traveled for a year and did not seclude, so when he came, he secluded himself.” \twenty nights\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3288","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Abraham saying: I heard Al-Aswad bin Yazid saying: Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to strive hard in ten matters and did not strive hard in any other.”"
"3289","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, he said: She said: Aisha: “When the ten days of prayer came, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revived the night, woke up his family, and tightened the apron.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3290","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr and Al-Harith bin Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then my family woke me up and I forgot about it, so they searched for it in the past ten days.”"
"3291","Ishaq bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Abdul-Malik reported on the authority of Bishr bin Shuaib, who said: My father told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah told me that Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was shown the Night of Decree, then I forgot it, so seek it.” \In the past ten years\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"3292","Ali ibn Hajar reported, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit informed me, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to tell us about the Night of Decree, and two Muslim men approached each other and said: “I have gone out to command you about the Night of Destiny.” And so-and-so and so-and-so sought, and it was removed, and perhaps it will be good for you, so seek it on the nine, the seven, and the five.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3293","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid, who is Ibn Zurayi, told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, he said: Anas told us, on the authority of Ubadah, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to tell us On the night of Laylat al-Qadr, two Muslim men approached each other, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “I went out and I wanted to inform you of the night of Destiny, and so-and-so and so-and-so sought, and it was lifted, and perhaps it would be good, so seek it at the ninth, seventh, and fifth.” And the wording is by Ibn al-Muthanna (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3294","Muhammad bin Salamah narrated, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim narrated, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out in Ramadan and said: “I was shown this night two men touching, and she rose and touched her in the “The ninth, the seventh, and the fifth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3295","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Salem informed me, that Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Some of you were shown that it is in the first seven, and some of you were shown “It is nine, seven, and five.”"
"3296","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Salem informed me, that Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Some of you were shown that it was in the first seven, and some people were shown Of you is that it is among the seven hidden things, so seek it out among the seven hidden days.”"
"3297","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw men from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in a dream that Laylat al-Qadr was in the last seven days of Ramadan, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I hear your vision. She agreed that it is in the last seven days, so whoever is searching for it should search for it in the last seven days.”"
"3298","Muhammad bin Salamah reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim reported, saying: Malik told me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw Laylat al-Qadr in a dream during the last seven nights, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I see that your visions have coincided in the last seven days, so whoever is investigating them should investigate them in the last seven days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3299","Muhammad bin Salamah narrated, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim narrated, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar narrated to me, on the authority of Abd God Ibn Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the Night of Decree is in the last seven nights.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3300","Muhammad bin Aqeel told me, on the authority of Hafs from Banu Salamah, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Damra bin Abdullah bin Unais, on the authority of his father, said: I was in a gathering of Banu Salamah, and I was the youngest of them, so they said: Who will ask? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us about Laylat al-Qadr, and that was the twenty-first morning of Ramadan? So I came and led the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Maghrib prayer, then I went to the door of his house, and he passed by me and said: “Come in,” so I went in. Then his dinner was brought, and you saw me refraining from it because of his lack of it. When he finished, he said: “Give me my sandal.” So he got up and I stood with him. He said: “As if you had a need.” I said: Yes, a group of Banu Salamah sent me to you asking you about Laylat al-Qadr. He said: How many nights? I said: Twenty-two. He said: “It is tonight,” then he came back and said: “Or the midwife.” He meant the night of the twenty-third. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Musa ibn disagreed with him. Jacob (Peace Be Upon Him)"
